-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by Jon Attree in JNext through the real loader,
              2026-11-04 (door fix and QAOP + Space)

  Replay      Original-game lockstep IDENTICAL on walk1, walk2 and t, default
              and Enhanced: 22513824 paired hook events, v1.1 run alongside.
              1764/1820 sampled frames pixel-identical to v1.1; the others
              differ only inside door/furniture cells where v1.1 shows the
              room colour and v1.2 the scenery colour, and at t frame 155
              (v1.1 menu icons left on the cleared screen). The figure painter
              writes no attribute (checked at every painter instruction);
              v1.1's vacated-cell writes and a restored entered-cell write
              both fail it. The frame-152 menu clear (0x80B4) is hooked:
              v1.1's 272 unhooked writes left menu icons as sprites for 7
              frames. t ends inside a plot (3/16 and 2/16 rows), which is left
              unchecked. 1483 unit cases per set; 6 earlier and 3 new
              negatives detected; 34 sites x 4 clocks x 2 sets pass.

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless, every frame of 900 in play, same keys:
              one-frame attribute changes in the play area v1.1 63 frames /
              119 cells, v1.2 0 / 0, both colour sets. Bare default, bare
              Enhanced and both menu builds reach play. No hardware test. No
              on-device NXC-loader test.

  Coverage    Same target, loading screen, default and Enhanced pattern bytes,
              trainers and credit as v1.0/v1.1. v1.1 hook-speed engine plus:
              the figure painter's nine LD (HL),E vacated-cell writes are NOPs
              (as its LD (HL),D writes already were), and the whole-screen
              clear 0x80B4 is hooked. Original game logic, sound and delays
              byte-exact; the only changed game-bank bytes are those ten
              sites.

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
